://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-02T19:00:36Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T19:00:36Z","body":"Recording of the [Starter Kit 3D Platformer](https://github.com/GodotVR/Starter-Kit-3D-Platformer) running at 72fps\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b766f2cc-2674-4b38-9121-727d6369617e","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5959383006/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5959433712","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124106#issuecomment-5959433712","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124106","id":5959433712,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYzW98A","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-02T19:02:48Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T19:02:48Z","body":"As can be seen in the recordings, the (subjective) experience when running an XR game as a bounded spatial container is that the smaller fov occupied by the bounded spatial container enables a good and pleasant experience at lower framerate than typically recommended for fully immersive XR experiences.\n\nFrom the recordings, similar to regular flat games, `30fps` seems to be a good minimum for a pleasant experience for contents running in a spatial container. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5959433712/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5963827798","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124106#issuecomment-5963827798","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124106","id":5963827798,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABY3jKVg","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-03T00:53:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-03T00:53:05Z","body":"I think it's not just the smaller FOV that helps here, it's also that the experience is placed infront of the player.\n\nIn an immersive experience, the player is likely to use the full 360 degree surroundings, with rapid head and body movement to look at things coming from every direction. Reprojection with frame synthesis can only do so much in this situation, so keeping framerates high becomes paramount to a pleasant experience.\n\nBut in this scenario, the player will be focused on the playing field infront of them, head movements will be much more constraint, with the visual data in a render being more than sufficient that reprojection alone can compensate.\nPlus the ability to see the real world, either due to the use of optical AR glasses or through passthrough, keeps the player anchored.\n\nIt would be interesting to repeat this experiment with the spatial container placed on a real world table, with the player walking around the table (very common with RPG type games like Demeo). In this scenario I think we can still provide comfortable experiences at low frame rates, but it will probably break once we hit things like 5fps.\n\nTLDR though, experience of this type do not have the high framerate requirements fully immersive games have.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5963827798/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]